==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[syneresis]] {{qualifier|US}}, [[synæresis]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|συναίρεσις||unification|sc=polytonic|tr=sunairesis|lang=grc}}, from {{term|συν||together|sc=polytonic|tr=sun|lang=grc}} + {{term|αἵρεσις||taking|sc=polytonic|tr=airesis|lang=grc}}, from {{term|αἱρέω||I take|sc=polytonic|tr=aireō|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/sɪnˈɛrəsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|synaereses}}
{{examples-right|sense=linguistics, prosody|examples=contraction of the ''-ew'' ({{IPA|/uː/|lang=en}}) and ''or-'' ({{IPA|/oʊɹ/|lang=en}}) of ''[[w:New Orleans|New Orleans]]'' into {{IPA|/ˈˈˈnɔːˈˈˈlənz/|lang=en}}.}}
# {{context|linguistics|prosody|lang=en}} the [[contraction]] of two [[vowel]]s into a [[diphthong]] or a [[long vowel]].
# {{context|chemistry|lang=en}} the [[separating]] out of the [[liquid]] from a [[gel]].

====Hypernyms====
*{{sense|linguistics|prosody}} [[metaplasm]]

